name wordnet-exceptions
# The exception lists. wndb.5: "Exception lists are alphabetized lists of inflected forms of words and their base
# forms. The first field of each line is an inflected form, followed by a space separated list of one or more base
# forms of the word. There is one exception list file for each syntactic category."
# The names given the fields here are wndb.5's words for them, this recipe's handles; they are in no claim.
match noun.exc verb.exc adj.exc adv.exc

tier row by \n
names inflected "base forms..."
tier field by space

thing row inflected
content inflected "base forms"
# each base form the line lists: wndb.5, "inflected forms of words and their base forms": [diastemata, base form,
# diastema]
relation "base form" "base forms"
attest row "base forms"
# The syntactic category the file is the exception list of (noun.exc: noun) is said by the file's name only, and a
# file's name is never a part of a claim: an unresolved obligation. The category as a part of the claim, a value of
# WordNet's syntactic categories (n, v, a, r), wants a part the recipe can take from the file (Laplace-Engine#32).
relate row {file} to ...
